  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Mixed Armor" id="dade-2d82-e565-0a18" hidden="false">
      <description>When the Ork player makes armor saves before removing casualties from a unit that has models with different armor saves he uses the best armor saves as long as the Orks wearing that type of armor are in the majority. Any casualties removed after saving throws have been take must come from amongsth the most heavily armored Orks first.
If heavier armored Orks are in the minority use the worse armor saves and take the casualties from the lightly armored Orks instead.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ork Mob Rule!" id="1586-dbe5-3b2e-7590" hidden="false">
      <description>If an Ork mob fails a moral or pinning check, roll 2D6. On a roll equal to or less than the number of Orks (ignore Gretchin) left in the mob than the Orks instead pass the test. An Ork mob of twelve or more models will therefore always pass these tests.
Orks falling back can attempt to regroup as normal, but may also instead fall back towards any Ork mob that lies behind their position. If any Orks in the withdrawing unit get within 6&quot; of the new mob once moves are complete then the withdrawing mob attempts to join with the new one. Roll 2D6 again the Leadership value of the falling back mob. If successful the two mobs combing together into one unit. The previously withdrawing mob can immediately move up to 6&quot; to be in coherency with the second unit.
Only Ork foot units will mob up in this manner. Slavers and Meks in Grot mobs or Big Gunz, Stormboyz and Warbikes may not mob up.
A mob of Orks that mobs up with another unit counts as destroyed for victory points purposes.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="The Power of the WAAAGH!" id="7bb4-34ca-51f3-bb8c" hidden="false">
      <description>When an Ork mob charges into close combat roll a 2D6. If the score is equal to or under the number of Orks in the mob they charge in with a rousing &quot;Waaaaaaaaagh!&quot;. All the Orks in the mob double their Initiative characteristic for the remainder of the assault phase. In future phases their Initiative returns to normal.
Orks who make sweeping advanced into the enemy also tests for The Power of the WAAAGH!. The test is made at the beginning of the assault phase so any casualties from enemy first will reduce the chances of them maintaining their momentum.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Gretchin Mobs" id="496b-e8d5-33fe-9edb" hidden="false">
      <description>Gretchin who fail a Moral check caused by enemy shooting or tank shock or which fail to regroup after falling back from close combat the grots &quot;go to ground.&quot; Remove all of the gretchin models from the board. If no slaver is present the mob is destroyed. If a slaver is present they remain on the board and attempts to regroup each turn, even if the Gretchin mob had been reduced below 50% starting strength or the enemy are within 6&quot; 
The slaver trying to regroup the Gretchin mob cannot move, shoot or initiate an assault, but can be shot at or charged. They fight back in close combat as normal. If the slaver is killed the Gretchin unit is now destroyed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Slippery" id="60e6-4b60-c541-3afb" hidden="false">
      <description>Kommandos sneak through cover quickly and easily, so they roll an extra D6 when they move through difficult ground.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tank Hunters" id="249e-3d2c-b96b-7edc" hidden="false">
      <description>The mob always passed Tank Shock tests and adds +1 to all Armor Penetration rolls.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Living Shield" id="cd1b-12a9-0ceb-301d" hidden="false">
      <description>Any Ork mobs which are shot at &quot;through&quot; a Grot mob can claim a 5+ cover save. Each successful save causes a Grot to be removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Better Footing" id="39ee-155c-f8e8-f5c1" hidden="false">
      <description>If a Grot mob is in difficult ground any Ork mobs moving through the same difficult ground my re-roll the dice for how far they move. Mega Armored Orks may not use this ability.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mine Clearance" id="c948-4917-842b-6b56" hidden="false">
      <description>If a Grot mob moves into a minefield remove 3D6 Grots as casualties and then remove the minefield marker. If there are fewer Grots remaining in the mob than the rolled dice than the Grot mob is destroyed and the minefield is not removed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Bailin&apos; Out" id="d491-6e1b-3887-ae83" hidden="false">
      <description>Trukk Boyz suffer a wound on a D6 roll of 6 instead of a 4+ if their Trukk is destroyed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Short Ranged" id="1487-add8-d98b-7898" hidden="false">
      <description>Warbike&apos;s Big Shootas are limited to a maximum rang eof 18&quot;.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hard to Hit" id="d2e0-6a69-f681-96f4" hidden="false">
      <description>Due to dust and exhaust clouds Warbikes give their riders a 5+ cover saving throw. Furthermore a unit being shot at &quot;through&quot; the warbikes also receive the 5+ cover saving throw.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Speed Freeks" id="8495-8dc4-d36b-5f4e" hidden="false">
      <description>Warbike Mobz are immune to the effects of morale and pinning.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Psycho Blastas" id="2502-cef3-ea93-ab5d" hidden="false">
      <description>In an assault Warbikers use their big shootas to blast the enemy at point blank range. Warbikers that charge into close combat strike first and make a shooting attack in the first round of combat instead of fighting normally.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hits on the Battery" id="8921-5e15-774b-8939" hidden="false">
      <description>When a battary of Big Gunz is fired at, randomize any hits between the krew and the gunz. Roll a D6:
1-4: Hits the Krew
5-6: Hits a Big Gun
Hits against the Gunz is treated like a vehicle with an armor value of 10, but any glancing or penetrating hits destroy them.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Looted Weapons" id="61d8-84e4-5a1f-6657" hidden="false">
      <description>If a 1 is rolled to hit with a looted weapon the hit is scored on the shooting unit instead of the target.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Looted Vehicles" id="e650-1e91-c401-41a1" hidden="false">
      <description>Make a Breakdown test for each looted vehicle at the start of each turn. On a result of 1 on a D6 roll another D6. On a 1 the vehicle may not move this turn, and automatically fails their Breakdown test next turn. On the result of 2-3 the vehicle may not move this turn. On the result of 4-6 the vehicle lurches directly foward 2D6&quot;. Make Dangerous Terrain, Tank Shock, etc. as if the vehicle were moving normally. The vehicle may not making any further moves this turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Choppa" id="aa19-c270-13f1-6356" hidden="false">
      <description>In close combat an enemy model wounded by a Choppa has a maximum armor save of 4+. Any 2+ or 3+ armor saves are instead reduced to 4+. Armor saves of 5+, 6+ or - are not changed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="More Dakka" id="173b-0e54-5eea-964e" hidden="false">
      <description>More Dakka kustomisin&apos; makes a shoota or slugga Assault 2 instead of rapid fire or pistol. A More Dakka kustom job combined with a Shootier kustom job  would produce a S5, Assault 2 shoota or slugga.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Shootier" id="bc5b-2941-29a7-ce0b" hidden="false">
      <description>Shootier weapons makes a shoota or slugga S5 instead of S4.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Blasta" id="9907-7c8b-718f-0156" hidden="false">
      <description>A shoota or slugga with the Blasta kustom job increases the armor piecing to AP3 at targets up to 12&quot; and AP2 at targets up to 6&quot;. But a shoota or slugga with the Blasta kustom job gains the Get Hot! rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="&apos;Eavy Armor" id="e312-e1c4-31fb-733d" hidden="false">
      <description>An Ork wearing &apos;Eavy Armor has a 4+ Armor Save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Grot Bombs" id="4a24-7d6e-a253-5ace" hidden="false">
      <description>Treated as a Smart Bomb. You may re-roll the scatter dice if you don&apos;t like the first result, but you must accept the second result.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
