    <selectionEntryGroup name="Ork Vehicle Upgrades" id="7ab0-3a69-56f8-540b" collapsible="true" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true">
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="Armor Plates" id="b3dd-d230-371f-07f9" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="5a3e-b584-f9e0-9979" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="5"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Armor Plates" id="05d7-c801-0fc3-5653" hidden="false">
              <description>Roll a D6 for each glancing or penetrating hit caused against the vehicle. On a 6 the hit is ignored.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Big Grabber" id="9b1d-140c-8cce-e2cf" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="4383-b412-fc4d-168a" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="5"/>
          </costs>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="or">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="f2f9-3e63-0705-0d93" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                    <condition childId="b73d-0887-9593-4929" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Big Grabber" id="d6c5-148b-4ec0-c322" hidden="false">
              <description>An Ork vehicle with a Big Grabba make attack an enemy vehicle in close combat. The Ork vehicle must move into contact with the target vehicle during its movement phase but may not attack if it moved more than 12&quot;.
The Ork vehicle may shoot in the shooting phase as normal and then resolves an attack in the assault phase. The vehicle has one attack for each upgrade listed (Big Grabber/Wrecker Ball/Reinforced Ram/Boarding Plank). Attacks hit on a 4+ regardless of the target&apos;s speed and are resolved with a Strength of 6. Walkers, skimmers, infantry and any other models that have a WS characteristic may not be attacked by these weapons.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Boarding Plank" id="5878-83d4-3a16-11f1" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="23f7-c076-d622-a2f4" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="5"/>
          </costs>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="or">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="f2f9-3e63-0705-0d93" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                    <condition childId="b73d-0887-9593-4929" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Boarding Plank" id="8a77-acf4-abc9-f8f5" hidden="false">
              <description>An Ork vehicle with a Big Grabba make attack an enemy vehicle in close combat. The Ork vehicle must move into contact with the target vehicle during its movement phase but may not attack if it moved more than 12&quot;.
The Ork vehicle may shoot in the shooting phase as normal and then resolves an attack in the assault phase. The vehicle has one attack for each upgrade listed (Big Grabber/Wrecker Ball/Reinforced Ram/Boarding Plank). Attacks hit on a 4+ regardless of the target&apos;s speed and are resolved with a Strength of 6. Walkers, skimmers, infantry and any other models that have a WS characteristic may not be attacked by these weapons.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Grot Riggers" id="2309-5dc2-c674-cd3d" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="95dc-839d-8f54-f5d9" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
            <constraint id="034b-d1ab-39cf-4354" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="min" value="0"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="2"/>
          </costs>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="or">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="f2f9-3e63-0705-0d93" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                    <condition childId="b73d-0887-9593-4929" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
            <modifier field="034b-d1ab-39cf-4354" type="set" value="1">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="7ae7-ec32-6af0-2290" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Grot Riggers" id="2f97-6fb2-4f85-64f4" hidden="false">
              <description>An immobilised Ork vehicle with Grot Riggers on board may make a test at the start of each Ork turn. Roll a D6, on a result of 4+ the immobilised status is removed.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Bolt-on Big Shoota" id="219d-edbd-d8ac-9e36" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="8853-f688-a6d9-f5ae" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="10"/>
          </costs>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="54fe-3f68-d142-362b" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="notInstanceOf" value="0"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Bolt-on Big Shoota" id="20d6-a08c-d905-0dfc" hidden="false">
              <description>A bolt-on big shoota can only be mounted on a wartrukk. It can be fired by one of da boyz onboard who is a passanger as long as the wartrukk itself does not move more than 12&quot; that turn.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Red Paint Job" id="cfb7-2ae5-d9ee-32c6" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="6896-2e95-0168-902a" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="3"/>
          </costs>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="or">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="f2f9-3e63-0705-0d93" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                    <condition childId="b73d-0887-9593-4929" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Red Paint Job" id="f483-f0b8-373b-ed5d" hidden="false">
              <description>An Ork vehicle with a red paint job adds +1&quot; to all of its move distances. For example, a fast Ork vehicle with a red paint job could move 13&quot; and still fire one weapon and/or disembark troops, or move 25&quot; and not fire at all.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Reinforced Ram" id="9d90-6c2e-f6c0-b8a5" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="ca35-f431-d666-78e5" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="5"/>
          </costs>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="or">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="f2f9-3e63-0705-0d93" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                    <condition childId="b73d-0887-9593-4929" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Reinforced Ram" id="9bef-9038-cb77-ddbc" hidden="false">
              <description>An Ork vehicle with a Big Grabba make attack an enemy vehicle in close combat. The Ork vehicle must move into contact with the target vehicle during its movement phase but may not attack if it moved more than 12&quot;.
The Ork vehicle may shoot in the shooting phase as normal and then resolves an attack in the assault phase. The vehicle has one attack for each upgrade listed (Big Grabber/Wrecker Ball/Reinforced Ram/Boarding Plank). Attacks hit on a 4+ regardless of the target&apos;s speed and are resolved with a Strength of 6. Walkers, skimmers, infantry and any other models that have a WS characteristic may not be attacked by these weapons.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Searchlight" id="d18d-c3c9-8ddc-6d2c" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="a201-34bd-fd32-9421" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="1"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Searchlight" id="da1f-a404-cc21-3cf9" hidden="false">
              <description>Searchlights are only used in missions where the rules for night fighting are being used. They allow one enemy unit spotted by the vehicle or Dreadnought to be fired at by all other Ork units that are in range and have a line of fire. However, the vehicle or Dreadnought using the Searchlight in this manner is considered visible to all enemy units who have line of sight on the next turn.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Spikes &apos;n Blades" id="b867-f671-19fa-ca39" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="36b1-5531-b287-d894" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="5"/>
          </costs>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="or">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="f2f9-3e63-0705-0d93" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                    <condition childId="b73d-0887-9593-4929" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="54fe-3f68-d142-362b" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Spikes &apos;n Blades" id="2352-a577-ca88-f7ba" hidden="false">
              <description>Enemy infantry which try to attack a vehicle that has spikes &apos;n blades in close combat and miss suffer a S3 hit.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Stikkabomb Chucka" id="94b7-9970-6ce9-57dd" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="4c8b-2703-73a7-b74a" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="3"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Stikkabomb Chucka" id="0cfd-4b78-658e-d07d" hidden="false">
              <description>A vehicle or Dreadnought equipped with stikkbomb chuckas can make a Tank Shock attack even though it isn&apos;t a tank. A vehicle may not move more than 12&quot; and attempt to tank shock and a Dradnought can only attempt a Tank Shock attack in its movement phase. In the assault phase it must move into close combat instead. If a proper tank is equipped with stikkbomb chuckas any tank shock it inflicts has an extra -1 modifier to the troop&apos;s Morale check.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Turbo Boosta" id="6066-7be1-f552-a410" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="4982-402d-b4d7-7ff0" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="5"/>
          </costs>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="or">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="f2f9-3e63-0705-0d93" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                    <condition childId="b73d-0887-9593-4929" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Turbo Boosta" id="4e51-00f3-0af5-dcfd" hidden="false">
              <description>A vehicle with turbo boostas can trigger them in any of its movement phases. The trubo boostas add D6&quot; to its movement, but for shooting and disembarking troops the vehicle counts as moving at the speed it went before the turbo boosters were added. The extra D&quot; movement must be used to move in a straight line and if a 4+ is rolled the vehicle and any passengers onboard may not shoot or disembark that turn as they are too busy hanging on for grim death.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Wrecker Ball" id="1968-0665-94dc-5fe7" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="e92f-ed99-d674-c4f7" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="5"/>
          </costs>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="or">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="f2f9-3e63-0705-0d93" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                    <condition childId="b73d-0887-9593-4929" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Wrecker Ball" id="24f4-a556-d019-7a16" hidden="false">
              <description>An Ork vehicle with a Big Grabba make attack an enemy vehicle in close combat. The Ork vehicle must move into contact with the target vehicle during its movement phase but may not attack if it moved more than 12&quot;.
The Ork vehicle may shoot in the shooting phase as normal and then resolves an attack in the assault phase. The vehicle has one attack for each upgrade listed (Big Grabber/Wrecker Ball/Reinforced Ram/Boarding Plank). Attacks hit on a 4+ regardless of the target&apos;s speed and are resolved with a Strength of 6. Walkers, skimmers, infantry and any other models that have a WS characteristic may not be attacked by these weapons.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Armoured Top" id="dfb0-e6ca-d747-dc06" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" page="10" publicationId="2b63-6841-db19-e6fa" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="712d-5adb-2f01-9f2e" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="8"/>
          </costs>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="7ae7-ec32-6af0-2290" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="notInstanceOf" value="0"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Armoured Top" id="53c9-ed36-b6a5-9f05" hidden="false" page="10" publicationId="2b63-6841-db19-e6fa">
              <description>Some Ork vehicles have an armoured roof, enclosed weapon turrets, etc. A vehicle with this upgrade no longer counts as being open-topped.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Force Field" id="cd9f-065e-7b8c-21dd" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" page="10" publicationId="2b63-6841-db19-e6fa" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="c5ef-f014-271d-1321" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="5"/>
          </costs>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="7ae7-ec32-6af0-2290" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="notInstanceOf" value="0"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Force Field" id="9ec7-94a7-47c6-683b" hidden="false">
              <description>The vehicle still counts as being open-topped but no longer suffers the +1 modifier to its Damage rolls. If the vehicle was a Fast type before, it loses this ability due to the power drained by the generators.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
